<!--
  Skip-to-content link. Renders as the very first focusable element on the
  page so keyboard and screen-reader users can bypass the nav and jump
  straight to the article. Visually hidden until focused (see .skip-link
  CSS in each theme).

  The target is `#main-content` — every layout sets that id and
  `tabindex="-1"` on its <main> so the link can move focus there. Don't
  remove the tabindex; without it, browsers won't focus a non-interactive
  element after the anchor jump and screen readers lose context.
-->
<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
